(290746, '_transient_feed_0d102f2a1f4d6bc90eb8c6ffe18e56ed', 'a:6:{s:5:\"child\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:3:\"rss\";a:1:{i:0;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:3:\"\n\n\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:7:\"version\";s:3:\"2.0\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:7:\"channel\";a:1:{i:0;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:49:\"\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n	\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n	\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:7:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"The Events Calendar\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:30:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:42:\"WordPress event plugins for awesome people\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:13:\"lastBuildDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Fri, 23 May 2025 23:53:05 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"language\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5:\"en-US\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:9:\"generator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:30:\"https://wordpress.org/?v=6.8.1\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"item\";a:10:{i:0;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:63:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:45:\"Pre-Event to Post-Event Engagement Strategies\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:52:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-engagement/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Mon, 26 May 2025 14:00:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:3:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"Blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:16:\"Event Management\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2547963\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:596:\"<p>If you’re an event planner that hasn’t been hiding under a rock for the last five years, you know — running successful events is not easy anymore.&#160; Traditional events struggle with getting people through the door and keeping them interested once they&#8217;re there. Virtual and hybrid events are dealing with &#8220;Zoom fatigue,&#8221; those awkward &#8220;can...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-engagement/\">Pre-Event to Post-Event Engagement Strategies</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:16:\"Nathan B. Weller\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:36934:\"\n<p>If you’re an event planner that hasn’t been hiding under a rock for the last five years, you know — running successful events is not easy anymore.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Traditional events struggle with getting people through the door and keeping them interested once they&#8217;re there. Virtual and hybrid events are dealing with &#8220;Zoom fatigue,&#8221; those awkward &#8220;can you hear me?&#8221; moments, and the lack of coffee break conversations in a digital space.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The silver lining is, when you nail event engagement, you build a real connection between attendees, what you&#8217;re sharing, and all the good stuff happening. That&#8217;s how you turn folks from just showing up to being total fans who can&#8217;t wait for the next one.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>So, in this guide, we’re sharing some tips to keep your crowd engaged from start to finish. We hope you can use these event engagement strategies to create memorable experiences that resonate long after the event ends.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-how-to-build-pre-event-excitement-and-drive-attendance\"><strong>How to build pre-event excitement and drive attendance</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Pre-event engagement involves creating buzz, setting expectations, and getting your attendees excited about what&#8217;s to come. Here are some ways to go about it!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-1-create-a-landing-page-for-your-event\"><strong>1. Create a landing page for your event</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Your event landing page needs to grab attention and provide all the essential information in one place. Key elements your landing page must include are:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>A compelling event description that highlights unique value.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Clear date, time, and location details.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Speaker profiles and photos.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Interactive schedule display.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Easy-to-spot registration button.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Don&#8217;t forget to add an FAQ section that answers common questions before they&#8217;re asked. Address everything from parking information to dietary accommodations — this shows you&#8217;ve thought about your attendees&#8217; needs and helps build trust. Place your <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-management/wordpress-event-registration/\">event registration</a> button prominently on the page, making it impossible to miss.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"789\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-665x789.png\" alt=\"Typical layout and elements of an event landing page\" class=\"wp-image-2547346\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-665x789.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-253x300.png 253w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-72x85.png 72w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-768x911.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-430x510.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-645x765.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-1068x1266.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-460x545.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-1074x1273.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-512x607.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-929x1102.png 929w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-447x530.png 447w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-600x711.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-500x593.png 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress.png 1190w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.optimizepress.com/\"><em>OptimizePress</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If you’re organizing multiple events, or have several different sessions during the course of an event, mapping them out on a calendar-type display makes it very easy for attendees to find and reserve the sessions they’re interested in.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The Events Calendar’s <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/event-schedule-manager/\">Event Schedule Manager plugin</a> makes this incredibly easy for <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/\">WordPress</a> users. With Event Schedule Manager, you can create stunning event pages that display your schedule in an easy-to-read format, complete with speaker sessions, breaks, and networking opportunities.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-2-set-up-a-powerful-registration-and-ticketing-system\"><strong>2. Set up a powerful registration and ticketing system</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Nobody loves filling out forms, so make your registration process painless and even exciting. <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-management/build-a-ticketing-website/\">Your ticketing system</a> should have multiple ticket tiers that cater to various attendee needs, from early birds who love a good deal to VIPs who want the full experience.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Want to boost group registrations? Create special packages that make it attractive for teams to attend together and sprinkle in some discount codes that make people feel like they&#8217;re getting an insider deal.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Keep things simple with a streamlined checkout that doesn&#8217;t ask for someone&#8217;s life story.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-3-use-email-marketing-to-increase-interest\"><strong>3. Use email marketing to increase interest</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Once someone registers, keep the excitement building through strategic email communication. <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/promoter\">Send personalized messages</a> based on their interests, rather than generic reminders, to make attendees feel special.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Your email campaign should include:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Speaker spotlights and interviews.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sneak peeks of workshop content.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Behind-the-scenes updates.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pre-event surveys and polls.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Sending out pre-event surveys helps understand audience expectations <em>and</em> makes attendees feel invested in the experience. However, make sure to convey genuine value in each email, while building anticipation, else you might see unsubscriptions or worse, be moved to the spam folder!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-4-hype-it-up-on-social-media\"><strong>4. Hype it up on social media</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Social media is your megaphone for event promotion, and using it right can create serious buzz. Start by creating a catchy event hashtag that&#8217;s easy to remember and unique to your event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Keep your social feeds active with engaging content like:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Behind-the-scenes photos of event preparations.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Quick video interviews with speakers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Countdown posts with exciting reveals.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Success stories from previous events.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Pay attention to what people are saying about your event online. When someone asks a question or shares their excitement, jump in and engage with them.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-5-host-pre-event-contests-and-create-fomo\"><strong>5. Host pre-event contests and create FOMO</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Nothing gets people excited quite like the chance to win something awesome. Create buzz by offering prizes that your audience really wants. This could be free passes to your event, exclusive VIP experiences, or even special meet-and-greets with keynote speakers.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Make your contests fun and simple to enter. Ask participants to share why they&#8217;re excited about your event or have them tag friends who might be interested. The key is to keep entry requirements easy while maximizing engagement.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Display registrants publicly (with permission) to leverage social proof. The psychology is simple: when people see others excited about attending, they don&#8217;t want to miss out. So, as registration numbers grow, FOMO will create a sense of urgency that <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/how-to-increase-ticket-sales-for-an-event/\">drives ticket sales</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-6-connect-with-industry-influencers-for-paid-marketing\"><strong>6. Connect with industry influencers for paid marketing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Finding the right influencers for <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-marketing-plan/\">marketing your event</a> can amplify your event&#8217;s reach to exactly the right audience. Look for voices that your target attendees already know and trust. These aren&#8217;t necessarily the people with the most followers, rather they&#8217;re the ones with the most engaged and relevant audiences in your industry.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Give your chosen influencers an inside look at what makes your event special. Provide them with exclusive content, early access to event features, or special interview opportunities with speakers.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>When they share their genuine excitement about your event, their followers are more likely to take notice and register. Track their impact by creating unique promotional codes for each influencer, helping you measure which partnerships drive the most registrations.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-in-event-strategies-for-peak-engagement\"><strong>In-event strategies for peak engagement</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Your attendees have arrived, and now it&#8217;s time to deliver on all the excitement you&#8217;ve built up. The key to keeping engagement high during your event is to create opportunities for active participation rather than passive attendance. Here&#8217;s how to keep the energy flowing and your attendees fully involved throughout your event.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-7-design-spaces-that-encourage-interaction\"><strong>7. Design spaces that encourage interaction</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"444\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-665x444.jpg\" alt=\"Group of people having discussions\" class=\"wp-image-2547492\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-665x444.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-300x200.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-127x85.jpg 127w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-768x512.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-480x320.jpg 480w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-240x160.jpg 240w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-720x480.jpg 720w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-430x287.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-645x430.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-460x307.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-512x342.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-707x472.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-600x400.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington-500x334.jpg 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/micro-events-comcast-washington.jpg 799w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/77474698@N07/34791272124/\"><em>Comcast Washington on Flickr</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Your venue layout should be a carefully crafted experience that guides attendees naturally from one meaningful interaction to the next. Start by mapping out high-traffic zones strategically. Place registration desks where they won&#8217;t create bottlenecks, and position networking areas near refreshment stations to encourage casual conversations over coffee or snacks.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Create Instagram-worthy photo spots featuring your event branding, and balance lively networking areas with quieter spaces for those who need to recharge.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember that every inch of your venue communicates something about your event. Make sure it&#8217;s saying what you intend through thoughtful design, signage, and accessibility considerations.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-8-craft-a-flexible-attendee-centered-agenda\"><strong>8. Craft a flexible, attendee-centered agenda</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Not every attendee is looking for the same thing from your event. Some might be focused on learning technical skills, while others want to build leadership abilities. That&#8217;s why a one-size-fits-all agenda rarely delivers the best experience. Instead, create a flexible program that lets attendees chart their own course through your event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Use an event app that allows personal schedule creation, and clearly categorize sessions to help people find relevant content.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Mix up your session formats to keep energy levels high throughout the day. For example, you could have:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>45–60-minute keynotes for big ideas.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>30-minute lightning talks for quick insights.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>90-minute workshops for hands-on learning.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>20-minute breaks for networking and reflection.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>For those who can&#8217;t attend every session they&#8217;re interested in, or for your virtual participants, record key presentations and make them available on-demand.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-9-choose-dynamic-speakers-and-optimize-your-setup\"><strong>9. Choose dynamic speakers and optimize your setup</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Great content needs great delivery to make an impact. When selecting speakers, find presenters who can turn complex ideas into compelling stories. The best speakers don&#8217;t talk at their audiences, but rather create conversations and experiences that stick.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Help your speakers with their presentations by:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Providing clear guidelines about your audience&#8217;s interests and needs.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Scheduling pre-event practice sessions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sharing tips for creating interactive moments.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Setting expectations for slide design and visual aids.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Encourage your presenters to think beyond traditional lectures. Ask them to weave in audience participation every 15–20 minutes, whether through quick polls, partner discussions, or hands-on exercises.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-10-use-seating-arrangements-that-promote-engagement\"><strong>10. Use seating arrangements that promote engagement</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Forget rows of chairs all facing forward; modern events need <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/types-of-seating-arrangement/\">innovative seating that gets people talking</a>. The way you arrange your space can make the difference between a room full of passive listeners and an energized group of active participants. Think about how furniture can help create the connections you want to see at your event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Round tables naturally encourage conversation, making them perfect for workshop sessions where you want attendees to share ideas. For networking events, mix in some high-top tables where people can gather casually, and create cozy corner setups with comfortable chairs where smaller groups can have focused discussions.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-11-allow-for-breaks-between-sessions\"><strong>11. Allow for breaks between sessions</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Back-to-back sessions might seem efficient on paper, but they can leave your attendees feeling drained and overwhelmed. Strategic breaks are valuable opportunities for processing information, making connections, and staying energized throughout your event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Plan your schedule with breathing room between activities. But don&#8217;t just leave attendees to figure out breaks on their own. Make these intervals count by offering structured options that add value to their experience:</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Consider providing:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Quiet zones for checking emails or making calls.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Guided stretching or meditation sessions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refreshment stations that encourage casual networking.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Some of the most valuable connections happen during these informal moments. When attendees are relaxed and refreshed, they&#8217;re more likely to engage meaningfully with your event content and with each other.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-12-offer-event-swag-and-unique-experiences\"><strong>12. Offer event swag and unique experiences</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>A branded pen and notepad as event memorabilia is a thing of the past. Event participants now expect memorable items and experiences that add real value. Make your swag count by focusing on items that attendees will actually use and appreciate, such as:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Eco-friendly water bottles with your event branding.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Digital resources they can access anytime.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Interactive experiences at sponsor booths.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Options to donate to meaningful causes.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Turn swag into an engagement tool by creating a rewards program. When attendees join discussions, complete surveys, or connect with sponsors, they can earn points toward exclusive merchandise or VIP experiences. This drives participation and also makes receiving swag more meaningful.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-13-host-inclusive-q-amp-a-panels\"><strong>13. Host inclusive Q&amp;A panels</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Q&amp;A sessions don&#8217;t have to be a game of fastest-hand-wins. Transform these valuable moments into truly inclusive conversations where every attendee has a chance to be heard.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Modern event apps let attendees submit their questions digitally throughout the session, while others upvote the ones they find most interesting, ensuring you address the topics your audience cares about most.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Build panels that reflect your diverse audience. When attendees see speakers who share their experiences and backgrounds, they&#8217;re more likely to engage with the discussion. A skilled moderator can weave these different perspectives together, keeping the conversation flowing while making sure every panelist gets equal time to share their insights.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-14-add-an-element-of-gamification\"><strong>14. Add an element of gamification</strong></h3>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"334\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-665x334.jpg\" alt=\"Graphic representing meaningful gamification that drives attendee interest and promotes networking \" class=\"wp-image-2547493\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-665x334.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-300x151.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-140x70.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-768x385.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-1536x771.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-2048x1028.jpg 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-430x216.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-645x324.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-2000x1003.jpg 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-1068x536.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-460x231.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-1602x804.jpg 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-1074x539.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-512x257.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-1611x808.jpg 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-707x355.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-600x301.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/gamification-graphic-500x251.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n<p>Gamification taps into our natural love of challenges and rewards. Create point-based activities for attending sessions, networking, or visiting exhibitors. Display real-time leaderboards to spark friendly competition, and design scavenger hunts that encourage exploration of your entire event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Winners can unlock exclusive experiences like VIP access to speakers, premium seating at popular sessions, or special sponsor merchandise. This kind of playful approach makes the event more fun, encourages active participation, and helps attendees get more value from their experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-15-offer-interactive-activities\"><strong>15. Offer interactive activities</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Passive learning is so yesterday. Today&#8217;s attendees want to roll up their sleeves and dive into hands-on experiences that teach them something valuable.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"443\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-665x443.jpg\" alt=\"A man wearing a VR headset and writing on a tablet as an example of integrating AR/VR into live event activities\" class=\"wp-image-2547498\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-665x443.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-300x200.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-128x85.jpg 128w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-768x512.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-2048x1365.jpg 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-480x320.jpg 480w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-240x160.jpg 240w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-720x480.jpg 720w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1528x1016.jpg 1528w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-764x508.jpg 764w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-430x287.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-645x430.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-2000x1333.jpg 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1068x712.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-460x307.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1602x1068.jpg 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1074x716.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-512x341.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1611x1074.jpg 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-1653x1102.jpg 1653w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-707x471.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-600x400.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/man-using-vr-headset-500x333.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/photo/a-man-using-digital-tablet-5213141/\"><em>Pexels</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Start with practical workshops where participants can develop new skills they&#8217;ll actually use in their daily work. These sessions should be small enough for everyone to get personal attention and practice what they&#8217;re learning.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>When attendees work together, whether they&#8217;re solving a business case study or participating in a group design challenge, these shared experiences create lasting connections and memorable learning moments.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-16-identify-live-entertainment-opportunities-where-possible\"><strong>16. Identify live entertainment opportunities where possible</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Who says professional events can&#8217;t be fun? Break up the serious stuff with carefully chosen entertainment that energizes your audience. Imagine starting your morning keynote with an acoustic performance that sets the perfect mood, or using a brief comedy segment to wake everyone up after lunch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can even showcase local talent to add authentic flavor to your event. A cultural performance during breaks or a digital art installation in the networking area can spark conversations and keep energy levels high.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-17-support-holistic-attendee-needs\"><strong>17. Support holistic attendee needs</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Remember that your attendees are whole humans with varying needs throughout your event. Offer mindfulness sessions such as guided meditation, breathing exercises, or stress-relief workshops to help attendees reset.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Complement these with thoughtfully designed quiet zones featuring comfortable seating, plenty of greenery, and soft lighting to create a serene atmosphere. Offer options for physical activity like stretch breaks or walking meetings to keep energy levels high.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Thoughtful food and beverage options accommodate diverse dietary needs while creating natural gathering points. Make sure your menu offers options for vegetarians, vegans, gluten-free diets, and religious requirements like halal or kosher.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-18-use-technology-thoughtfully\"><strong>18. Use technology thoughtfully</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Real-time insights are invaluable when it comes to understanding attendee behavior and optimizing your event. With non-invasive tools, you can track engagement without disrupting the experience. RFID or NFC-enabled badges, for instance, can automatically log session attendance and booth visits, providing critical data on what’s resonating with your audience.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>On the very high tech (and high expense) end, it’s possible to analyze audience sentiment using AI-powered tools that track facial expressions during keynotes and sessions. These insights can help you measure how impactful your content is and make adjustments on the go. Heat-mapping technology is another excellent tool to see which areas of your venue attract the most traffic and adjust your event flow dynamically.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"353\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-665x353.jpg\" alt=\"Ethical facial and behavior analysis using tools like Zenus AI\" class=\"wp-image-2547499\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-665x353.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-300x159.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-140x74.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-768x408.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-1536x815.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-430x228.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-645x342.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-1068x567.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-460x244.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-1602x850.jpg 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-1074x570.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-512x272.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-1611x855.jpg 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-707x375.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-600x318.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai-500x265.jpg 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/facial-analysis-zenus-ai.jpg 1824w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.zenus.ai/\"><em>Zenus AI</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Maintain high production quality with excellent audiovisuals, smooth transitions, and thorough testing of all systems. For virtual or hybrid components, use multiple camera angles and interactive elements to create a dynamic experience for remote participants.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Switching perspectives keeps the sessions dynamic, making the experience more engaging for remote participants. Smooth transitions between sessions are equally important — use moderators or pre-recorded video segments to maintain energy and flow between agenda items.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To avoid unnecessary hiccups, run extensive technical rehearsals in advance. These dry runs help identify and fix potential issues so everything runs seamlessly on the big day.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-post-event-success-converting-attendees-into-brand-advocates\"><strong>Post-event success: Converting attendees into brand advocates</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The event may be over, but your work is far from done. Post-event <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/community-event-management/\">community engagement</a> is where you turn satisfied attendees into loyal advocates for your brand. Here’s how you can nurture relationships, gather valuable feedback, and ensure a continued connection.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-19-maintain-post-event-communication\"><strong>19. Maintain post-event communication</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Just because the event has ended doesn’t mean the conversation has to stop. Keep attendees engaged by reaching out with thoughtful follow-ups. A personalized thank-you email is a great place to start — include highlights of the event, key takeaways, and links to recorded sessions for those who couldn’t attend everything.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can use tools like <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/promoter\">Promoter</a> to create data-driven follow-up campaigns that segment attendees based on their engagement patterns and interests.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"238\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-665x238.jpg\" alt=\"Promoter add-on landing page.\" class=\"wp-image-2544867\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-665x238.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-300x107.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-140x50.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-768x275.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-1536x550.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-2048x734.jpg 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-430x154.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-645x231.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-2000x717.jpg 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-1068x383.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-460x165.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-1602x574.jpg 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-1074x385.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-512x183.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-1611x577.jpg 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-707x253.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-600x215.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/07/promoter-home-page-500x179.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n<p>Engage a broader audience by creating an event debrief page. This page can feature presentation slides, networking opportunities, and downloadable resources, offering continued value to attendees while giving non-attendees a reason to explore your brand.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-20-measure-and-improve-post-event-engagement-metrics\"><strong>20. Measure and improve post-event engagement metrics</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Data tells stories that impressions alone can&#8217;t capture. Start by collecting and analyzing key metrics such as registration rates, session attendance, and engagement levels during the event. These numbers give you a clear snapshot of your event’s success.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Post-event surveys are another powerful tool for gathering qualitative feedback. Ask attendees what they loved, what could be improved, and whether they’d attend another event. Use this feedback to identify trends, refine your strategies, and improve future experiences. Metrics and attendee insights together can help you make data-driven decisions that elevate your next event.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Compare results against pre-event goals to identify both successes and opportunities for improvement.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-putting-it-all-together-your-complete-engagement-strategy\"><strong>Putting it all together: Your complete engagement strategy</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>So, what’s the next step? Start by reflecting on how you want your attendees to feel when they leave your events. Inspired. Energized. Connected. Use these goals to shape every aspect of your engagement plan, from how you build excitement before the event to the steps you take to foster relationships afterward.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To make this process easier, we’ve put together an <strong><a href=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/10/tec-nonprofit-event-planning-checklist.pdf\">event planning checklist (PDF, 5MB)</a></strong> designed to guide you through every stage of creating unforgettable experiences. Download it today and start turning your vision into reality, one step at a time!</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-engagement/\">Pre-Event to Post-Event Engagement Strategies</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:1;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:63:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:71:\"Event Tickets Update Delivers New Onboarding Wizard and Settings Design\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:107:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-tickets-update-delivers-new-onboarding-wizard-and-settings-design/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Thu, 22 May 2025 17:38:39 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:3:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"Blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:10:\"What\'s New\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548962\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:649:\"<p>We&#8217;ve got another exciting product update to share with you this week. On Monday, we released a new version of Event Tickets that provides new users with a seamless onboarding experience and existing users with a settings design refresh we think you&#8217;ll love. Let’s take a look! An Overview of Event Ticket’s New Onboarding Wizard...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-tickets-update-delivers-new-onboarding-wizard-and-settings-design/\">Event Tickets Update Delivers New Onboarding Wizard and Settings Design</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:16:\"Nathan B. Weller\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:18816:\"\n<p>We&#8217;ve got another exciting product update to share with you this week. On Monday, we released a new version of Event Tickets that provides new users with a seamless onboarding experience and existing users with a settings design refresh we think you&#8217;ll love.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Let’s take a look!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>An Overview of Event Ticket’s New Onboarding Wizard</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Upon activation of Event Tickets, new users are now met with the welcome screen below. You can take four actions here:</p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Select your location:</strong> this is where you sell your tickets. It’s important that this information is accurate because it impacts which payment gateways you can use.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Proceed to next screen:</strong> this will initiate the onboarding process. However, you may want to opt into sharing information about your plugin usage so we can use it to make improvements in the future (see 4).</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Skip guided setup:</strong> this allows you to skip the onboarding process altogether. You might find this process unnecessary if you’ve already set up Event Tickets many times.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Opt in to data sharing:</strong> this checkbox permits us to collect data on plugin usage to improve it in the future. It’s a free and easy way to make your own and the rest of the community’s experience better.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfnvieOWgUEqXAtLhPHJLAVZ3OLJcoQpQZYEnnChzuKOaOrcKt9fHauvHNmeLFwB5K6jGjltA2nRRIJKtAaDMJyBqMUwTD329ci3xWCTYqoDul-AhnDfnCCKkIaJWVwBj2QKFnF?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Once you click the “Setup your tickets” button, the onboarding process begins. At this stage, you select your currency and connect to Stripe. PayPal is also available once you get to the settings area (after the onboarding process), and more payment gateway options are coming soon.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXfveh7ReKaqyTxEd93qjnloRg84M0JH0qy-5g1C10ocMANDKw9QYVthrzif0m7B6VvSxXY6AyRDNkXvvzeCc9NWSE5doPx-bPSsYN96MtG_dTFkhfPHcTaOa8OandfxU0zDyiSk?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Next up is the Communication screen. This is where you set the email address and sender name for the emails your website sends to customers.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1472\" height=\"1918\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548995\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1.jpg 1472w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-230x300.jpg 230w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-665x866.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-65x85.jpg 65w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-768x1001.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-1179x1536.jpg 1179w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-600x782.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/et-onboarding-and-settings-design-refresh-5-1-500x651.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1472px) 100vw, 1472px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Finally, we have the Events screen. This screen will look different depending on whether you have already installed The Events Calendar. If you do not have it installed, you will be prompted to install it, which the wizard will do for you.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXceryiJw2jiEDL-zEWm5vkci0BpmA8__VmREpbnBVmlv0fTrx0NazbcAdSBt-W_wKn5-BRq0FfexxDx4veJwekI1AorcJfZI9mjKgctDBWeQ-VFALwhHY3O92rvq8SyCNyX4rcZQQ?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>If The Events Calendar is installed, you will be prompted to go through its onboarding wizard or to finish configuring the Event Ticket settings in the WP Admin.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXdD9QvEyrNoSU7DqFsoFgg76brwM4-8CHnvXxa6BYuxXUNstbS_1pBo1gU4wKz7sy_AZtZ28Nw4re_kVZEonFbjkjrhONM9cPKuzypo9ziIliiP6E-2aG4MVP9iR0xZbqGfHjuknw?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Which brings us to Event Tickets’ new settings design!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Event Tickets Settings Design Refresh</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>This is an update we’ve been excited about for a long time. The Events Calendar got its settings design glow-up back in September, and we’ve been eager to do the same for Event Tickets, too. Let’s take a look at the before and after.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The Old Look</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXc7eRjxID6F1KNrl1N87crpH3O_wlXzu0kpKC3blil_-m5j9EVMJpLHlVKl8_dS-eKuQeFZOEb-LyluRm7syiMQtoFRCHlprY8wAV7fXNwnHZ0U17JGIGcp37rJrIFtVggq_0rDnQ?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The old design above was meant to align closely with the standard WordPress backend user interface, maintaining a consistent user experience from screen to screen in the WP Admin. Since then, however, both WordPress and users&#8217; design expectations have changed a lot. We knew we needed to update our settings to provide a cleaner design and simpler, more accessible user experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>The New Look</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://lh7-rt.googleusercontent.com/docsz/AD_4nXf5fD1LkYdVrvEvlgsn7DNnkHcm0Nt3LON5Vndg1CbnjxXFVtU8P-_PGVrLVAXHH8Onsw0JaJTPLBQWD7k3Dg6O4bR8Qr7gvcEAvPm9l6omSMOmoCnkF0J4UyLnJLF1QL9phvCXrA?key=iP9tr5ZwyeNTiqi-gxSvvQ\" alt=\"\"/></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Our new design removes a lot of visual clutter and offers improved responsiveness. The most significant structural change was removing the help links and resources from the top of the main settings page and placing that content in a sidebar. This keeps those resources present regardless of your settings tab while simplifying the visual hierarchy on the general settings screen. It’s now also much easier for anyone using accessibility mode to navigate the WP Admin to tab through Event Tickets settings.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>More Product Updates Coming Soon!</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>With these updates, we aim to provide a more streamlined and intuitive experience for all users, whether setting up Event Tickets for the first time or managing their existing settings. Stay tuned for even more enhancements and features in the upcoming releases as we continue to improve and refine our products.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-in-case-you-missed-it\">In Case You Missed It <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f50d.png\" alt=\"🔍\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f440.png\" alt=\"👀\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>We&#8217;re always working to make our product suite better for you. Below are just three, recent examples, of new features we&#8217;ve released that bring new functionality to our products while making your life easier. To see all major feature and product releases, check out our <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/category/blog/news/\">full news feed</a>. If you&#8217;d like to see all product updates, including maintenance and security releases, you can find that information in our <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/category/release-notes/\">release notes</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-qr-code-generations-now-built-in-to-the-events-calendar\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">QR Code Generations Now Built-in to The Events Calendar</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"411\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-665x411.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547944\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-665x411.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-300x186.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-137x85.png 137w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-768x475.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-1536x950.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-430x266.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-645x399.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-1068x661.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-460x285.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-1602x991.png 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-1074x664.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-512x317.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-1611x997.png 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-707x437.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-600x371.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2-500x309.png 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/TEC-QR-Code-Generation-Featured-Image-64798-01-2.png 1636w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>This feature automatically generates QR codes for every event you publish. These codes can be downloaded and used across digital and physical marketing materials (think posters, flyers, jumbotrons, and more.) No long URLs or confusion, just instant access.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2548962_afc158-ce\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2548962_e00da7-c7 kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/qr-codes-are-here-connect-promotional-material-to-your-event-calendar-with-ease/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn about QR Code Generation!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">Embed Your Events Calendar on Any External Website</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"410\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-665x410.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547581\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-665x410.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-300x185.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-138x85.jpg 138w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-768x474.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-430x265.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-645x398.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-1068x659.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-460x284.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-1074x663.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-512x316.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-707x436.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-600x370.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-500x309.jpg 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2.jpg 1528w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></a></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>You can now easily share your full events calendar beyond your main site! With our new embed feature, you can place your calendar on any external website to boost visibility.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2548962_9a287c-cf\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2548962_ddfa40-f9 kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn more about Calendar Embeds!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-offer-discounts-and-increase-sales-with-event-tickets-coupons\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">Offer Discounts and Increase Sales with Event Tickets Coupons</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/event-tickets-coupons/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"410\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-665x410.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547469\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-665x410.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-300x185.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-138x85.png 138w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-768x474.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-430x265.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-645x398.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-1068x659.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-460x284.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-1074x663.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-512x316.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-707x436.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-600x370.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-500x309.png 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2.png 1528w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></a></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>Give your attendees a little extra incentive to click &#8220;buy.&#8221; Our Event Tickets Coupons feature lets you create and manage discount codes directly within your dashboard. It&#8217;s a great way to drive ticket sales and reward your audience.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2548962_51ccf2-a9\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2548962_8ee980-8c kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/event-tickets-coupons/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn how to create ticket coupons!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-tickets-update-delivers-new-onboarding-wizard-and-settings-design/\">Event Tickets Update Delivers New Onboarding Wizard and Settings Design</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:2;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:26:\"The Events Calendar 6.13.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:91:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-13-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 20 May 2025 17:27:27 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"The Events Calendar\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548832\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:590:\"<p>Summary Feature Release The latest update of The Events Calendar adds a `Block_Trait` to simplify block assets registration and avoid code duplication. The Events Calendar 6.13.0 is only compatible with: As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✨ Feature Features in this release: ✅...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-13-0/\">The Events Calendar 6.13.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5639:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-normal-font-size\">Feature Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The latest update of The Events Calendar adds a `Block_Trait` to simplify block assets registration and avoid code duplication.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>The Events Calendar 6.13.0 is only compatible with: </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Events Pro 7.6.0 and higher</strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Events Community 5.0.7 and higher</strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Event Tickets 5.23.0 and higher</strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0 and higher</strong></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend<a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\"> testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-feature\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Feature</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Add a `Block_Trait` to simplify block assets registration and avoid code duplication.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"> <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Improve Settings UX by preventing unstyled error state when tab object does not exist. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update class steps to use namespaced class names consistently to improve class reusability. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>In the onboarding API, improve data management by merging new params instead of overwriting existing ones. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Standardize asset loading by using a consistent function to load assets.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks<br></h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release: </p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Alter Telemetry to allow classes to hook in and supress the modal for specific pages. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hide Telemetry modal on the onboarding page. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improve the onboarding wizard by properly storing current tab completion and adding filter to force redirect. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Replace `tribe_asset` with `tec_asset` function for proper asset pathing. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add `tec_events_onboarding_wizard_force_display` filter to allow bypassing Guided Setup display checks. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add `tec_events_onboarding_force_redirect_to_guided_setup` filter to bypass checks for redirecting to Guided Setup. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move Country and Currency lists to Common for better code reuse. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update asset handling to leverage group paths consistently.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>2 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>252 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>4 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>38 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/the-events-calendar/the-events-calendar-6-13-0/\">The Events Calendar 6.13.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:3;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:20:\"Event Tickets 5.23.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:79:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-23-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 20 May 2025 17:27:25 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Event Tickets\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548827\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:584:\"<p>Summary Feature Release The latest update of Event Tickets introduces an Onboarding Wizard for easier setup and a revamped Settings page that now matches The Events Calendar for a more cohesive experience. Read more about the Onboarding Wizard &#38; revamped Settings here! Event Tickets 5.23.0 is only compatible with: As always, we recommend testing updates...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-23-0/\">Event Tickets 5.23.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4048:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-normal-font-size\">Feature Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">The latest update of Event Tickets introduces an Onboarding Wizard for easier setup and a revamped Settings page that now matches The Events Calendar for a more cohesive experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read more about the Onboarding Wizard &amp; revamped Settings <a href=\"https://evnt.is/1beb\">here</a>!</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Event Tickets 5.23.0 is only compatible with: </strong></p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>The Events Calendar 6.13.0 or higher </strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0 or higher.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend<a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\"> testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Introduces the Event Tickets Onboarding Wizard.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Revamp Event Tickets Settings page to match The Events Calendar.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Add defensive coding to custom_glance_items_attendees() to avoid a fatal. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Change the asset loading function from `tribe_asset` to `tec_asset` in various parts of the codebase.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-css-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>58 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>361 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>2 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>6 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets/event-tickets-5-23-0/\">Event Tickets 5.23.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:4;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:57:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:15:\"Community 5.0.7\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:56:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/community-5-0-7/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 20 May 2025 17:27:23 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:10:\"What\'s New\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548824\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:539:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release The latest Community version corrects an issue where Admin Alerts would fatal when TEC was not active. Events Community 5.0.7 is only compatible with: As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✅ Fixes Bugs squashed in this release: ⚙️ Tweaks Tweaks...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/community-5-0-7/\">Community 5.0.7</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4326:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">The latest Community version corrects an issue where Admin Alerts would fatal when TEC was not active.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Events Community 5.0.7 is only compatible with</strong>:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>The Events Calendar 6.13.0 and higher.</strong></li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Event Tickets 5.23.0 and higher.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Correct an issue where Admin Alerts would fatal when TEC was not active.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Make sure update callbacks are executed prior `wp_loaded` action.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improve email alert templates with dedicated versions for TEC and Event Tickets integrations. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add helper functions for event labels that respect plugin integrations. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refactor email alert handling for better maintainability and extensibility. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Switch from using `tribe_tickets_plugin_loaded` to `tec_tickets_fully_loaded` for better Event Tickets compatibility. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Added template path filters to allow customizing email template paths.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Deprecate `sendEmailAlerts` method in favor of `send_email_alerts` with improved functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>3 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>40 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>1 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/community-5-0-7/\">Community 5.0.7</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:5;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:24:\"Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:88:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-5-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 20 May 2025 17:27:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:18:\"Event Tickets Plus\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548822\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:609:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release This version of Event Tickets Plus optimizes the Seating feature to properly register assets when on single-event pages and improves WooCommerce integration with assigned seating to display notice text more elegantly. Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0 is only compatible with Event Tickets 5.23.0 or higher. As always, we recommend testing updates on a...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-5-0/\">Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5040:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Event Tickets Plus optimizes the Seating feature to properly register assets when on single-event pages and improves WooCommerce integration with assigned seating to display notice text more elegantly.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0 is only compatible with Event Tickets 5.23.0 or higher.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Optimize the Seating feature to properly register assets when on single-event pages. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improve WooCommerce integration with assigned seating to display notice text more elegantly. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update JavaScript files throughout to use consistent formatting and coding standards. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Fix deprecated message display for assigned seating with WooCommerce. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update the plugin to use the new group paths system for assets.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Add support for horizontal layout blocks in settings pages for improved visual organization. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update styling for settings forms with new classes like `tec-settings-form__header-block` and `tec-settings-form__section-header`. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Update the Attendee Registration and Integrations settings pages with improved UI and clearer descriptions. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improve settings layout for WooCommerce integration with better organization and clearer messaging. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Move email footer credit setting to appear before `tec-settings-email-email-styling-wrapper-end`. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consolidate the Tickets Commerce description to use paragraph formatting. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Eliminate duplicate vendor dependencies in asset loading by removing &#8216;tribe-tickets-plus-gutenberg-vendor&#8217;. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Rename asset group paths for better organization and more consistent naming. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Transitioned from `tribe_asset` to `tec_asset` for modern asset handling.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>109 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>1 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>1 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/event-tickets-plus/event-tickets-plus-6-5-0/\">Event Tickets Plus 6.5.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:6;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:25:\"Events Calendar Pro 7.6.0\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:90:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-6-0/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Tue, 20 May 2025 17:26:46 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"Events Calendar Pro\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548820\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:599:\"<p>Summary Feature Release This version of Events Calendar Pro optimizes asset loading with improved grouping and conditional logic, and block asset loading structure to improve performance. Events calendar Pro 7.6.0 is only compatible with The Events Calendar 6.13.0 or higher. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-6-0/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.6.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:5015:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Feature Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Events Calendar Pro optimizes asset loading with improved grouping and conditional logic, and block asset loading structure to improve performance.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Events calendar Pro 7.6.0 is only compatible with The Events Calendar 6.13.0 or higher.</strong></p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-features\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2728.png\" alt=\"✨\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Features</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Features in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Migrate our style and script building process to StellarWP. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Adds proper separation of asset paths for the build directory and packages. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Updated block asset loading structure for better performance.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Optimized asset loading with improved grouping and conditional logic.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-tweaks\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2699.png\" alt=\"⚙\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Tweaks</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Tweaks in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Changed all instances of `tribe_asset()` to `tec_asset()` for compatibility with the new asset system. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Updated asset registration paths to match the new build system structure. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Improved asset conditionals and organization across the plugin. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Updated Calendar embed block to use the new build path structure. </li>\n\n\n\n<li>Standardized CSS naming conventions with separate skeleton and full style files.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>154 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>2 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-6-0/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.6.0</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:7;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:63:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:46:\"Build a Profitable Hybrid Event Marketing Plan\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:58:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/hybrid-event-marketing/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Mon, 19 May 2025 14:00:00 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:3:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"Blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:16:\"Event Management\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2547953\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:590:\"<p>According to a study by Bizzabo, 97% of marketing professionals are betting big on hybrid events in the future. However, promoting a single event that delivers two distinct audience experiences is still a challenge.&#160; We’ve seen countless talented organizers pour their hearts (and budgets) into hybrid events, only to watch virtual attendees drop off or...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/hybrid-event-marketing/\">Build a Profitable Hybrid Event Marketing Plan</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:16:\"Nathan B. Weller\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:38753:\"\n<p>According to a study by Bizzabo, <a href=\"https://welcome.bizzabo.com/reports/evolution-of-events-report\">97% of marketing professionals</a> are betting big on hybrid events in the future. However, promoting a single event that delivers two distinct audience experiences is still a challenge.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>We’ve seen countless talented organizers pour their hearts (and budgets) into hybrid events, only to watch virtual attendees drop off or in-person guests feel disconnected.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>If unprecedented ROI, global reach, and lasting impact are what you are looking for with your next hybrid event, you need two things.</p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>A change in perspective. Look at hybrid events as a revenue multiplier rather than just an attendance booster. Start thinking about how you can use the format to create premium experiences while also scaling attendance.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Try out the battle-tested strategies we’ve listed below to create a <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-marketing-plan/\">profitable hybrid event marketing plan</a>. This covers audience segmentation, ticket pricing strategies, engagement tactics, and much more.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<p>Ready? Here’s how hybrid event marketing is done right.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-1-understand-target-personas-for-both-audiences\"><strong>1. Understand target personas for both audiences</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Hybrid events cater to two distinct groups: in-person attendees and virtual participants. Understanding their motivations, behaviors, and expectations is important for creating targeted marketing messages that resonate with each audience.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"483\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-665x483.png\" alt=\"Target personas for live and virtual event attendees\" class=\"wp-image-2547956\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-665x483.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-300x218.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-117x85.png 117w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-768x557.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1536x1115.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-2048x1487.png 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-430x312.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-645x468.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-2000x1452.png 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1068x775.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-460x334.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1602x1163.png 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1074x780.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-512x372.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1611x1169.png 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-1518x1102.png 1518w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-707x513.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-600x436.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/target-personas-500x363.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n<p>An effective marketing strategy begins with identifying and addressing each audience&#8217;s specific needs.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>In-person attendees</strong> typically seek:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Networking opportunities.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hands-on experiences.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Direct interactions with speakers and exhibitors. </li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>They value the energy of a live environment and often justify higher ticket prices for these benefits.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Virtual attendees</strong> prioritize:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Convenience.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Accessibility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>On-demand content. </li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>They appreciate the ability to participate without travel costs or time commitments while still gaining valuable information.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To develop effective marketing messages, use past event data, conduct surveys, and analyze social media insights to understand what each audience values most. Create detailed audience personas based on demographics, industry roles, and engagement preferences to guide your marketing efforts.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-2-set-different-expectations-for-both-types-of-attendees\"><strong>2. Set different expectations for both types of attendees</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Clear communication across all event touchpoints prevents confusion and <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/5-tips-for-increasing-virtual-event-engagement/\">improves attendee satisfaction</a>. When participants receive the experience they anticipated, engagement levels naturally increase.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ensure the hybrid nature of your event is highlighted in:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Event website and landing page</strong>: Clearly state that attendees can choose between in-person and virtual participation, with specific details about what each experience includes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Email invitations and social media promotions</strong>: Consistently reinforce the hybrid format to attract both audience types.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Registration forms</strong>: Include a mandatory field where attendees select their preferred participation mode to help with planning and personalized follow-up.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Using consistent language and visual cues (such as color-coded icons for in-person vs. virtual components) helps clarify the event format and set proper expectations.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Be specific about what each group will receive:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>In-person attendees</strong> will have venue access, face-to-face networking, physical exhibition booths, live Q&amp;As, and hands-on workshops.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Virtual attendees</strong> get access to livestreams, interactive chat functions, virtual networking rooms, on-demand content access, and digital resources.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Address common questions proactively:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Will virtual attendees have access to all sessions?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>How will networking work for remote participants?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Will in-person attendees also have digital access to event materials?</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Create a comprehensive FAQ section on your event website to reduce uncertainty and set clear expectations for both audience types.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-3-create-a-flexible-agenda\"><strong>3. Create a flexible agenda</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"996\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-665x996.webp\" alt=\"Image showing a structured program brochure for a business conference\" class=\"wp-image-2547958\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-665x996.webp 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-200x300.webp 200w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-57x85.webp 57w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-768x1150.webp 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-1026x1536.webp 1026w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-430x644.webp 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-645x966.webp 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-1068x1599.webp 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-460x689.webp 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-1074x1608.webp 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-512x767.webp 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-736x1102.webp 736w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-354x530.webp 354w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-1104x1653.webp 1104w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-534x800.webp 534w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program-500x749.webp 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/business-conference-program.webp 1200w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/photo/printout-papers-spiral-notebooks-and-badges-on-gray-surface-8761741/\"><em>Pexels</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>A well-structured, adaptable agenda ensures both audience groups can fully participate without logistical conflicts. Flexibility improves virtual engagement, accommodates time zone differences, and maximizes the reach of event content.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>When <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-management/how-to-create-hybrid-events-with-the-events-calendar/\">creating a hybrid event</a> agenda, consider:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Session duration</strong>: Virtual attendees typically engage better with shorter, focused sessions (30–45 minutes), while in-person attendees might prefer deeper dives (60–90 minutes).</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Daily session limits</strong>: Avoid digital fatigue by balancing educational sessions with networking opportunities and breaks.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Parallel tracks</strong>: Consider offering some separate sessions for in-person and virtual attendees alongside shared keynotes and main events.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Timing is crucial for hybrid events with global reach, so schedule key sessions during times that work for your primary audience regions. Offer important sessions more than once to accommodate different time zones and provide on-demand access for virtual attendees who cannot attend live sessions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Make recorded sessions available for later viewing to extend the life of your content and increase its value. Include interactive components throughout your agenda, such as live polls, Q&amp;A sessions, or virtual breakout rooms, to maintain engagement from both audience types.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Consider using a mix of live and pre-recorded content to balance real-time engagement with production quality and flexibility.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-4-choose-the-right-event-management-platform\"><strong>4. Choose the right event management platform</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Hybrid events require a robust platform that supports both in-person and virtual experiences. The right technology ensures smooth event management, enhances engagement, and simplifies logistics like registration, streaming, networking, and analytics.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Event organizers have two main options: using a dedicated event management platform or <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/creating-online-events-legacy/\">setting up their own hybrid event website</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-option-1-using-an-event-management-platform\"><strong>Option 1: Using an event management platform</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How it works</strong>: All-in-one event management platforms handle registration, live streaming, attendee engagement, analytics, and more.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"kb-table-container kb-table-container2547953_b8ddaf-bd wp-block-kadence-table\"><table class=\"kb-table kb-table2547953_b8ddaf-bd\">\n<tr class=\"kb-table-row kb-table-row2547953_9148df-ef\">\n<th class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_821861-7a\">\n\n<p><strong>Pros</strong></p>\n\n</2547953_821861-7a>\n\n<th class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_a103c4-b4\">\n\n<p><strong>Cons</strong></p>\n\n</2547953_a103c4-b4>\n</tr>\n\n<tr class=\"kb-table-row kb-table-row2547953_062198-bd\">\n<td class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_07df4d-ec\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Easy to set up and manage.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Built-in networking, engagement, and analytics tools.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reliable support and scalability.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</2547953_07df4d-ec>\n\n<td class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_752f7f-bf\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Monthly or per-event pricing can be expensive.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Limited customization options compared to self-hosted solutions.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</2547953_752f7f-bf>\n</tr>\n</table></div>\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Recommended event management platforms</strong>:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><a href=\"https://www.cvent.com/in\"><strong>Cvent</strong></a> is a comprehensive hybrid event solution with strong registration, networking, and analytics features.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://spotme.com/\"><strong>SpotMe</strong></a> focuses on audience engagement with interactive tools for both in-person and virtual attendees.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.bizzabo.com/\"><strong>Bizzabo</strong></a> is great for large-scale hybrid events with strong branding and customization options.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><a href=\"https://www.ringcentral.com/rc-events.html\"><strong>RingCentral Events</strong></a> (formerly Hopin) is known for its rich virtual networking and audience interaction features.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>For virtual streaming components, consider platforms like <a href=\"https://streamyard.com/\">StreamYard</a>, which offers professional broadcasting capabilities that integrate with major streaming services.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-option-2-setting-up-a-self-hosted-hybrid-event-website\"><strong>Option 2: Setting up a self-hosted hybrid event website</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How it works</strong>: Instead of using a third-party platform, organizers create their own hybrid event website.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"kb-table-container kb-table-container2547953_8b2739-ff wp-block-kadence-table\"><table class=\"kb-table kb-table2547953_8b2739-ff\">\n<tr class=\"kb-table-row kb-table-row2547953_eef3f4-4f\">\n<th class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_e5a891-df\">\n\n<p><strong>Pros</strong></p>\n\n</2547953_e5a891-df>\n\n<th class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_fd193d-76\">\n\n<p><strong>Cons</strong></p>\n\n</2547953_fd193d-76>\n</tr>\n\n<tr class=\"kb-table-row kb-table-row2547953_66dd43-45\">\n<td class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_13d1cb-36\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Full control over branding, content, and user experience.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cost-effective in the long run.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Complete integration with existing websites and marketing tools.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</2547953_13d1cb-36>\n\n<td class=\"kb-table-data kb-table-data2547953_6ec661-97\">\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Requires more setup and technical expertise.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Does not have built-in attendee networking and analytics tools.</li>\n</ul>\n\n</2547953_6ec661-97>\n</tr>\n</table></div>\n\n\n<div style=\"height:30px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></div>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Recommended self-hosted solution</strong>: <a href=\"https://wordpress.org/\"><strong>WordPress</strong></a><strong> + </strong><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/wordpress-events-calendar/\"><strong>The Events Calendar Suite</strong></a></p>\n\n\n\n<p>This combination of calendar, ticketing, seating, and marketing management tools creates a powerful foundation for hybrid event websites.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"387\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-665x387.jpg\" alt=\"The Events Calendar homepage\" class=\"wp-image-2545922\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-665x387.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-300x175.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-140x81.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-768x447.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1536x894.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-430x250.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-645x375.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1068x621.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-460x268.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1602x932.jpg 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1074x625.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-512x298.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1611x937.jpg 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-1894x1102.jpg 1894w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-707x411.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-600x349.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed-500x291.jpg 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2024/09/the-events-calendar-headshot-compressed.jpg 1978w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n<p>The Events Calendar Suite <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-management/build-a-ticketing-website/\">supports event registration and ticketing</a> while allowing for virtual session scheduling through integrations with video platforms. The extensive customization options let you match your brand identity and event goals perfectly.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-5-build-an-impactful-event-landing-page\"><strong>5. Build an impactful event landing page</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Your event landing page serves as the central hub for all event information and registration. It plays a key role in driving conversions by providing clear details and compelling reasons to attend. For hybrid events, this page must highlight the value of both in-person and virtual participation.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>The page should immediately communicate that your event offers both live and virtual attendance options. Use messaging that highlights the benefits of each format.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Include these essential event details, such as:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Event date, time, and location (for in-person attendees).</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Speaker lineup with photos and brief bios.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Session highlights and agenda preview.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Ticket pricing for both attendance types.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Sponsors and partners to add credibility.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Testimonials from past attendees to build trust.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"789\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-665x789.png\" alt=\"Typical layout and elements of an event landing page\" class=\"wp-image-2547346\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-665x789.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-253x300.png 253w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-72x85.png 72w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-768x911.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-430x510.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-645x765.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-1068x1266.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-460x545.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-1074x1273.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-512x607.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-929x1102.png 929w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-447x530.png 447w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-600x711.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress-500x593.png 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/event-landing-page-template-optimizepress.png 1190w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em>Source: </em><a href=\"https://www.optimizepress.com/\"><em>OptimizePress</em></a></figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Use engaging visuals and media, including high-quality images and speaker headshots, event teaser videos showing both in-person and virtual components, past event highlights demonstrating successful hybrid execution, and consistent branding and colors for visual appeal.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Ensure your landing page is mobile-friendly with responsive design, quick to load on all devices, accessible with clear fonts and good contrast, and easy to navigate with an intuitive layout.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Make sure to optimize your landing page for SEO and conversions. Here are some tips:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use relevant keywords related to your event, industry, and location.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Include a clear, compelling call-to-action (CTA) like &#8220;Reserve Your Spot Now&#8221;.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Simplify the registration process by asking only for essential information.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Create separate registration paths for in-person and virtual attendees.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-6-create-different-ticket-pricing-strategies-for-live-and-virtual-attendees\"><strong>6. Create different ticket pricing strategies for live and virtual attendees</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Hybrid events need tailored ticket pricing because the perceived value differs between virtual and live attendees. A structured pricing strategy ensures fair value for both experiences, encourages higher attendance, boosts revenue, and allows for targeted promotions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Offer multiple ticket categories to accommodate different budgets and needs. For example, you could have:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>In-person standard tickets</strong> with full access to venue sessions, networking, and workshops.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>In-person VIP tickets</strong> that include everything in standard tickets plus exclusive meet-and-greets, premium seating, and special perks.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Virtual basic tickets</strong> offering access to livestreamed keynotes and select sessions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Virtual premium tickets</strong> that have the basic features plus interactive Q&amp;As, virtual networking rooms, and on-demand access for 30–90 days.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Encourage upgrades by clearly highlighting the additional value of higher-tier tickets, such as exclusive content, extended access periods, or premium networking opportunities.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can also implement pricing incentives to maximize registrations, such as:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Early-bird discounts (15–25% off) with clear deadlines to drive early commitment.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Group discounts for teams of 3+ to encourage company-wide participation.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Bundle packages combining in-person and virtual access for flexible attendance.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Loyalty rewards, offering returning attendees special rates.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>For WordPress-based event sites, <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/wordpress-event-tickets/\">Event Tickets Plus</a> provides great functionality for creating multiple ticket types, managing registrations, and tracking sales. The plugin makes it super easy to implement tiered pricing and special offers while keeping everything organized.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Last but not least, set up <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/event-management/event-payment-processing/\">integrated payment gateways</a> and automated pricing rules to <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/how-to-sell-tickets/\">streamline ticket sales</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-7-have-a-virtual-first-marketing-strategy\"><strong>7. Have a virtual-first marketing strategy</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>A virtual-first marketing approach is necessary for hybrid events because they rely heavily on digital promotion to reach a broad audience. This strategy ensures that online attendees feel as valued as in-person participants while allowing for scalable outreach, personalized engagement, and measurable success.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>To create a successful digital-first marketing campaign, use multiple channels:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Social media</strong>: Build awareness and generate buzz through regular posts highlighting speakers, sessions, and engagement opportunities.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Email marketing</strong>: Nurture leads with value-focused content and send timely reminders as the event approaches.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Content marketing</strong>: Publish blog posts, guest articles, and video teasers that showcase event topics and speakers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Paid ads</strong>: Target specific audience segments with tailored messaging to boost conversions.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Ensure all promotional messaging clearly communicates hybrid attendance options and their respective benefits. Use urgency-driven CTAs like &#8220;Limited virtual seats available&#8221; or &#8220;Early-bird pricing ends Friday&#8221; to encourage prompt sign-ups.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-identify-the-best-social-channels-for-event-promotion\"><strong>Identify the best social channels for event promotion</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Not all social channels yield the same results. Select platforms based on your event&#8217;s industry and audience.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For instance, LinkedIn is best for B2B events and professional networking to share speaker announcements, industry insights, and thought leadership content. Twitter/X is great for industry discussions and real-time engagement. Create event hashtags and participate in relevant conversations. Instagram &amp; TikTok are ideal for visual promotions and influencer partnerships. Share behind-the-scenes content and short-form <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/effective-video-marketing-for-events/\">video content for better engagement</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Apart from these, email remains one of the most effective and personalized event promotion tools. Use a solution like <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/promoter/\">Promoter</a>, by The Events Calendar, for WordPress-based event websites to automate event reminders and follow-ups, segment lists to personalize outreach, and track open rates and conversions for optimization.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-connect-with-influencers-in-your-space-for-better-marketing-reach\"><strong>Connect with influencers in your space for better marketing reach</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>When was the last time you tried something new because your Insta role model recommended it? Quite recently, we bet!&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>A study by Matter Communications shows that <a href=\"https://www.marketingdive.com/news/influencer-marketing-success-matter-study-2023/643310/\">81% of people</a> are ready to buy a product if an influencer recommends it to them. With their massive fan followings, influencers have the power to hype up your event and make new audiences trust you, even if they might have never heard of you before.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Some ways to collaborate with influencers include:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Identify influencers whose audience matches your target attendees.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Offer exclusive perks like free access, VIP experiences, or paid partnerships.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Have them share event teasers and personal invitations.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Arrange for them to host sessions or interviews with key speakers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Request testimonials or endorsements to build credibility.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-8-maximize-engagement-across-both-experiences\"><strong>8. Maximize engagement across both experiences</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The success of hybrid events hinges on meaningful engagement between virtual and in-person participants. Remote attendees, in particular, need compelling reasons to stay actively involved throughout the event. Strategic planning and thoughtful execution can transform passive viewers into active participants, regardless of their location.</p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"483\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-665x483.png\" alt=\"Maximizing attendee engagement for both live and virtual audiences \" class=\"wp-image-2547959\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-665x483.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-300x218.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-117x85.png 117w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-768x557.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1536x1115.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-2048x1487.png 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-430x312.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-645x468.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-2000x1452.png 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1068x775.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-460x334.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1602x1163.png 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1074x780.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-512x372.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1611x1169.png 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-1518x1102.png 1518w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-707x513.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-600x436.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/04/hybrid-event-engagement-500x363.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></figure></div>\n\n\n<p>Use technology as the great connector. Add interactive polls and real-time chat features to keep virtual attendees connected to the main event, and have dedicated livestreaming setups for continued audio-visual communication between both audiences. Select tools that enhance rather than complicate the attendee experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Build a vibrant community. The most successful hybrid events extend beyond the scheduled programming. Consider creating dedicated digital spaces where connections can flourish:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Launch event-specific communities on <a href=\"https://slack.com/intl/en-in\">Slack</a> or <a href=\"https://discord.com/\">Discord</a>.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Maintain active social media presence with targeted hashtags.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Implement recognition programs celebrating engaged participants.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Offer incentives to boost participation. Digital badges, leaderboard rankings, and exclusive content rewards create healthy competition while encouraging meaningful interaction. However, don’t go overboard with the gamification. These elements should complement the event&#8217;s core objectives rather than overshadow them.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-create-meaningful-cross-audience-connections\"><strong>Create meaningful cross-audience connections</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Mixed-format activities that bring both audiences together can be a core attraction for hybrid events. Virtual breakout rooms, joint workshops, and buddy systems that pair live and virtual attendees based on common interests are some ways of doing this.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Design collaborative challenges that require input from both audience types, leading to natural interaction and knowledge sharing.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>You can set up regular touchpoints throughout the event to help maintain engagement and create opportunities for spontaneous connections, much like the chance encounters that make traditional events so valuable.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-9-offer-dedicated-support-to-virtual-attendees\"><strong>9. Offer dedicated support to virtual attendees</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>When virtual attendees encounter problems, every minute spent troubleshooting is a minute of lost engagement. Without dedicated support, connectivity problems, platform difficulties, or unclear navigation can lead to frustration and drop-offs.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>At the heart of your virtual support strategy should be a cross-functional team ready to tackle any challenge. <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/creating-a-virtual-event/\">Virtual event</a> hosts can serve as the friendly faces welcoming online attendees, while dedicated technical specialists stand ready to resolve streaming, login, and connectivity issues. Behind the scenes, experienced moderators can keep discussions flowing in chats and Q&amp;As, ensuring no question goes unanswered.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Think of offering proactive support before the event. Prevention is always better than cure. In the days leading up to your event, share these resources with your attendees.</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Pre-event guides with clear instructions on accessing sessions.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Troubleshooting tips for common technical issues.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Support contact information and available hours.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Platform orientation sessions to familiarize attendees with features.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>During the event, set up a live help desk to provide immediate assistance for urgent issues, and a dedicated support chat channel to offer quick solutions for simpler questions. Check in regularly to identify potential issues before they become problems.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Having an FAQ section with step-by-step solutions for common problems like login errors, audio issues, and session navigation is also a good idea.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-10-leverage-post-event-marketing-for-continued-engagement\"><strong>10. Leverage post-event marketing for continued engagement</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The event may be over, but your relationship with attendees shouldn&#8217;t end there. Effective post-event marketing helps maintain interest, build long-term connections, and <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/how-to-track-attendance-at-events/\">nurture future event attendance</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Start by creating a content package that includes session recordings, which can be particularly valuable for those who missed live sessions. Transform key moments into engaging highlight reels that capture the event&#8217;s energy and essential insights. This content serves as a valuable resource for attendees and is powerful marketing material for future events.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Gather feedback to improve future events. Send short, targeted surveys about session value, technical experience, and overall satisfaction. Ask specific questions about what worked well and what could be improved, and offer incentives like discounts on future events to encourage higher response rates.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>Keep the momentum going with thoughtful follow-up communication. Send personalized thank-you messages that include:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Key event takeaways and memorable moments.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Links to recorded sessions and additional resources.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Invitations to join ongoing community discussions.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>Finally, maintain engagement by introducing upcoming opportunities, whether they&#8217;re webinars, networking events, or early registration for your next major gathering.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-start-planning-your-hybrid-event-marketing-strategy-today\"><strong>Start planning your hybrid event marketing strategy today</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Hybrid events present both challenges and opportunities. Now is the time to refine your marketing strategy using the approaches outlined in this article to maximize attendance, optimize engagement, and create a memorable experience.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/bundles/bundle-ultimate/\">Experiment with different hybrid event platforms</a>, marketing tactics, engagement tools, and content formats to discover what resonates best with your audience. And if you need a WordPress event toolkit to get started, The Events Calendar suite is here to create and market hybrid events that drive results.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For more tips on how to build profitable hybrid events, <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/newsletter-signup/\">sign up for our newsletter</a>!</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/hybrid-event-marketing/\">Build a Profitable Hybrid Event Marketing Plan</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:8;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:60:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:27:\"Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0.1\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:92:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-5-0-1/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Thu, 15 May 2025 17:25:55 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:2:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:19:\"Events Calendar Pro\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"release notes\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2548676\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:598:\"<p>Summary Maintenance Release This version of Events Calendar Pro ensures that saving events with checkbox-type additional fields does not produce a fatal error. As always, we recommend testing updates on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing. ✅ Fixes Bugs squashed in this release: 🗣 Translations Updated language files and strings:</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-5-0-1/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0.1</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:13:\"Emily Negroni\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:2806:\"\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-summary\">Summary</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"release-label has-normal-font-size\">Maintenance Release</p>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"release-summary__overview has-medium-font-size\">This version of Events Calendar Pro ensures that saving events with checkbox-type additional fields does not produce a fatal error.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>As always, we recommend <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/knowledgebase/k/creating-and-using-a-wordpress-staging-site/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">testing updates</a> on a staging site first, but it should all be smooth sailing.</p>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-fixes\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/2705.png\" alt=\"✅\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Fixes</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Bugs squashed in this release:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Ensures that saving events with checkbox-type additional fields does not produce a fatal error.</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-9d6595d7 wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.3%\">\n<h4 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-translations\"><img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f5e3.png\" alt=\"🗣\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> Translations</h4>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p class=\"has-medium-font-size\">Updated language files and strings:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>0 new strings added</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 updated</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 fuzzied</li>\n\n\n\n<li>0 obsoleted</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/release-notes/events-calendar-pro/events-calendar-pro-7-5-0-1/\">Events Calendar Pro 7.5.0.1</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}i:9;a:6:{s:4:\"data\";s:63:\"\n		\n		\n		\n		\n		\n				\n		\n		\n		\n\n					\n										\n					\n		\n		\n			\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";s:5:\"child\";a:3:{s:0:\"\";a:6:{s:5:\"title\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:80:\"QR Codes are Here! Connect Promotional Material to Your Event Calendar with Ease\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:115:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/qr-codes-are-here-connect-promotional-material-to-your-event-calendar-with-ease/\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:7:\"pubDate\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:31:\"Thu, 15 May 2025 16:37:01 +0000\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:8:\"category\";a:3:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"Blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:1;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:10:\"What\'s New\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}i:2;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"blog\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:4:\"guid\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:40:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/?p=2547928\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:1:{s:11:\"isPermaLink\";s:5:\"false\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:11:\"description\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:684:\"<p>Today 72% of event planners consider QR codes a must-have in their event toolkit. That&#8217;s why, with the latest update to The Events Calendar, we’ve rolled out built-in QR code generation– a feature designed to bridge the gap between your digital calendar and real-world experiences. Whether you manage conferences, concerts, or community events, this new...</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/qr-codes-are-here-connect-promotional-material-to-your-event-calendar-with-ease/\">QR Codes are Here! Connect Promotional Material to Your Event Calendar with Ease</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:32:\"http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/\";a:1:{s:7:\"creator\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:14:\"Sarah Zuercher\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:40:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/\";a:1:{s:7:\"encoded\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:27485:\"\n<p>Today <a href=\"https://www.eventmanagerblog.com/\">72% of event planners consider QR codes a must-have</a> in their event toolkit. That&#8217;s why, with the latest update to <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/products/wordpress-events-calendar/\">The Events Calendar</a>, we’ve rolled out built-in QR code generation– a feature designed to bridge the gap between your digital calendar and real-world experiences. Whether you manage conferences, concerts, or community events, this new feature makes it easy to connect your audience to the right information at the right time.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\n<iframe loading=\"lazy\" title=\"New Feature! QR Code Generation for The Events Calendar\" width=\"720\" height=\"405\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/wkaKv-pgcy0?feature=oembed\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n</div></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Is This Made for You? (Spoiler: Yes!)</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>This feature automatically generates QR codes for every event you publish. These codes can be downloaded and used across digital and physical marketing materials (think posters, flyers, jumbotrons, and more.) No long URLs or confusion, just instant access.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>For users of Events Calendar Pro, this feature includes <strong>dynamic series QR codes that automatically redirect attendees to the next upcoming event in a recurring series</strong>. So instead of updating and reprinting materials every month, you can use one evergreen code all season long.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>This feature is built for <em>you</em>. It’s especially useful if you want to:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Bridge physical and digital event promotion</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Provide instant access to event info, registration, and more</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Integrate QR code functionality seamlessly into your event creation workflow</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Limit manual entry errors and friction for attendees</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Reduce printing costs with evergreen marketing assets</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Share events quickly across a variety of platforms</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">4 Smart Ways to Use QR Codes</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>QR codes can make your job easier and your event planning smoother. Whether planning a massive conference or a cozy community meetup, QR codes can do more than just point to an event page. Let’s explore creative and innovative ways to make the most of them.</p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Promote Recurring Events Without Reprinting: </strong>Festival promoters or music series organizers can save serious time and printing costs by using dynamic series QR codes. Print one code on all materials and it can automatically direct fans to the next upcoming event.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Connect Print Materials to Online Ticketing: </strong>Theater directors can use QR codes on posters, flyers, and programs to link directly to show details. It makes it easy for patrons to go from interest to purchase in seconds.&nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Maximize Space on Flyers: </strong>University events managers dealing with limited poster space can use QR codes to pack in more information—event details, RSVP links, calendar add-ons—without cluttering up the design.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Turn Tables into Promo Tools: </strong>Restaurant owners can boost attendance for special events by adding QR codes to receipts, menus, or table tents. Diners can scan to see upcoming wine tastings, live music nights, or chef’s dinners.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Using the Event Calendar’s New QR Code Feature</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Based on customer feedback we know that many of our users depend on third party solutions for QR code generation–especially if they need dynamic QR codes for recurring events or event series. With this feature we have made QR code generation and management as simple as a few clicks within your WP Admin.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Generate and Download QR Codes</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>To get your QR code for an event, go to <strong>Events</strong> → <strong>Events</strong>. Hover over the event and select <strong>Generate QR Code.</strong> After a code has been generated for an event, this text will read “View QR Code.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1334\" height=\"786\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548404\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1.jpg 1334w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-300x177.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-665x392.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-140x82.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-768x453.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-600x354.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image1-1-500x295.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1334px) 100vw, 1334px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>A popup will appear in the middle of your screen. Download the PNG by selecting the size (if different than the default) and hitting the <strong>Download</strong> button.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1334\" height=\"820\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548410\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6.jpg 1334w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-300x184.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-665x409.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-138x85.jpg 138w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-768x472.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-600x369.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image6-500x307.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1334px) 100vw, 1334px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Event QR codes can also be found on each event’s editor screen.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1334\" height=\"734\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548411\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8.jpg 1334w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-300x165.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-665x366.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-140x77.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-768x423.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-600x330.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image8-500x275.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1334px) 100vw, 1334px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>The two other areas Events Calendar Pro users will find QR codes available are under <strong>Events → Series</strong> and the editor screen for each series, same as the above example for single events. These QR codes are dynamic, which means the destination of the QR code changes over time. After each event in a series passes, the QR code will begin re-directing to the next event in the series.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">QR Code Block, Widget, and Shortcodes</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>There are some use cases in which you may want to use an event QR code on your website itself. You may be presenting or displaying your site on a large screen, for example. In those instances, you can use our new events QR code block, widget, and shortcodes.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Event QR Code Block</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>To add an Event QR Code to a page or post, add the Event QR Code Block.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1544\" height=\"834\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548412\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3.jpg 1544w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-300x162.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-665x359.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-140x76.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-768x415.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-1536x830.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-600x324.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image3-500x270.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1544px) 100vw, 1544px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>You’ll be able to:</p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Give your QR code a title</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Set its display size</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Choose where the code redirects to when scanned</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1334\" height=\"798\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548413\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4.jpg 1334w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-300x179.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-665x398.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-140x85.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-768x459.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-600x359.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image4-500x299.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1334px) 100vw, 1334px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>There are a few redirection options to choose from:</p>\n\n\n\n<ol class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Redirect to the current event:</strong> send users to the event that is currently happening. If there isn&#8217;t one, send them to the next future event.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Redirect to the first upcoming event:</strong> send users to the next future event on the calendar.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Redirect to a specific event ID:</strong> send users to a specific event you&#8217;ve selected.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Redirect to the next event in a series (Pro feature):</strong> send users to the next recurring event or event in a series.</li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<p>When you choose either of the last two options, a second dropdown will appear where you can choose the event you want to redirect to.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1518\" height=\"956\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548414\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9.jpg 1518w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-300x189.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-665x419.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-135x85.jpg 135w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-768x484.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-600x378.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image9-500x315.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1518px) 100vw, 1518px\" /><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Screenshot</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Once the Event QR Code Block is configured and saved, you’ll have a custom QR code on your website!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1334\" height=\"736\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548415\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7.jpg 1334w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-300x166.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-665x367.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-140x77.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-768x424.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-600x331.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image7-500x276.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1334px) 100vw, 1334px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Event QR Code Widget</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Our widget is just like the block. You can access it by navigating to <strong>Appearance → Widgets </strong>and then adding the<strong> Events QR Code</strong> wherever it makes sense.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1999\" height=\"942\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2548416\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2.jpg 1999w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-300x141.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-665x313.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-140x66.jpg 140w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-768x362.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-1536x724.jpg 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-600x283.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/05/image2-500x236.jpg 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1999px) 100vw, 1999px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Event QR Code Shortcodes</h3>\n\n\n\n<p>You also have the option of using a shortcode.</p>\n\n\n\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code\"><code>&#91;tec_event_qr mode=specific id=216 size=16]</code></pre>\n\n\n\n<p>The shortcode can be modified in a few specific ways:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>mode:</strong> current , upcoming, specific, next.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Id:</strong> if specific mode then it’s the event id and if next mode, then it’s the series id.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>size:</strong> integer from 1 to 28 (steps of 35px).</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Pro Tips for Marketing QR Codes</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Here are pro tips to make your QR codes effective:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Test it first: </strong>Make sure your code links to the correct event page! Nothing kills momentum like incorrect links.&nbsp;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Place them strategically:</strong> Near entrances, registration tables, or session doors– anywhere someone might pause or notice. Think beyond paper, too. QR codes work great on social media posts, digital signage, receipts, name badges, and merch!</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Pair with a call to action:</strong> Use action-oriented language. A QR code with a CTA like “scan to register” or “get the full schedule” can increase engagement.&nbsp;</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Combine with other channels:</strong> Use them in tandem with email, social media, direct mail, or packaging. QR codes shine when they’re part of a broader campaign, not the entire strategy.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to Add Scanning to Your Event Planning?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>QR codes are your new event sidekick. Let the QR codes do the heavy lifting by connecting your people to all your event details. Less printing, less friction, more engagement.&nbsp;</p>\n\n\n\n<p>So go ahead: share, scan, and simplify. Your future events (and your attendees) will thank you.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>We’ve got even more exciting features on the way, so don’t miss a beat. <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/newsletter-signup/\">Subscribe to our newsletter</a> and stay in the loop!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-in-case-you-missed-it\">In Case You Missed It <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f50d.png\" alt=\"🔍\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /> <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.1.0/72x72/1f440.png\" alt=\"👀\" class=\"wp-smiley\" style=\"height: 1em; max-height: 1em;\" /></h2>\n\n\n\n<p>We&#8217;re always working to make our product suite better for you. Below are just three, recent examples, of new features we&#8217;ve released that bring new functionality to our products while making your life easier. To see all major feature and product releases, check out our <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/category/blog/news/\">full news feed</a>. If you&#8217;d like to see all product updates, including maintenance and security releases, you can find that information in our <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/category/release-notes/\">release notes</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">Embed Your Events Calendar on Any External Website</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"410\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-665x410.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547581\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-665x410.jpg 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-300x185.jpg 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-138x85.jpg 138w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-768x474.jpg 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-430x265.jpg 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-645x398.jpg 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-1068x659.jpg 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-460x284.jpg 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-1074x663.jpg 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-512x316.jpg 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-707x436.jpg 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-600x370.jpg 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2-500x309.jpg 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/External-Calendar-Embed-64239-v2.jpg 1528w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></a></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>You can now easily share your full events calendar beyond your main site! With our new embed feature, you can place your calendar on any external website to boost visibility.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2547928_a9b34d-e1\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2547928_a71959-61 kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/embed-your-events-calendar-on-any-external-website/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn more about Calendar Embeds!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-offer-discounts-and-increase-sales-with-event-tickets-coupons\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">Offer Discounts and Increase Sales with Event Tickets Coupons</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/event-tickets-coupons/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"410\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-665x410.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547469\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-665x410.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-300x185.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-138x85.png 138w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-768x474.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-430x265.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-645x398.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-1068x659.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-460x284.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-1074x663.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-512x316.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-707x436.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-600x370.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2-500x309.png 500w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Event-Tickets-Coupons-64237-v2.png 1528w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></a></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>Give your attendees a little extra incentive to click &#8220;buy.&#8221; Our Event Tickets Coupons feature lets you create and manage discount codes directly within your dashboard. It&#8217;s a great way to drive ticket sales and reward your audience.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2547928_cdb953-6d\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2547928_bebc0c-cc kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/event-tickets-coupons/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn how to create ticket coupons!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-seating-is-compatible-with-woocommerce\" style=\"padding-bottom:20px\">Seating is Compatible with WooCommerce</h3>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-columns are-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-columns-is-layout-cb90e00a wp-block-columns-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:33.33%\"><div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/seating-compatible-with-woocommerce/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"665\" height=\"411\" src=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-665x411.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2547441\" style=\"aspect-ratio:1;object-fit:cover\" srcset=\"https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-665x411.png 665w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-300x186.png 300w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-137x85.png 137w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-768x475.png 768w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1536x950.png 1536w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-2048x1267.png 2048w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-430x266.png 430w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-645x399.png 645w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-2000x1237.png 2000w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1068x661.png 1068w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-460x285.png 460w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1602x991.png 1602w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1074x664.png 1074w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-512x317.png 512w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1611x997.png 1611w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-1781x1102.png 1781w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-707x437.png 707w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-600x371.png 600w, https://images.theeventscalendar.com/uploads/2025/03/Woo-Seating-Featured-Image-64238-01-500x309.png 500w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 665px) 100vw, 665px\" /></a></figure></div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-column is-vertically-aligned-center is-layout-flow wp-block-column-is-layout-flow\" style=\"flex-basis:66.66%\">\n<p>You asked, we delivered! Seating now fully integrates with WooCommerce. Sell tickets, choose seats, and process payments with WooCommerce—no add-ons or workarounds required.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-kadence-advancedbtn kb-buttons-wrap kb-btns2547928_25494a-c5\"><a class=\"kb-button kt-button button kb-btn2547928_bd8e5d-cd kt-btn-size-standard kt-btn-width-type-auto kb-btn-global-fill kt-btn-has-text-true kt-btn-has-svg-false wp-block-kadence-singlebtn\" href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/news/seating-compatible-with-woocommerce/\"><span class=\"kt-btn-inner-text\">Learn about WooCommerce for Seating!</span></a></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com/blog/qr-codes-are-here-connect-promotional-material-to-your-event-calendar-with-ease/\">QR Codes are Here! Connect Promotional Material to Your Event Calendar with Ease</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://theeventscalendar.com\">The Events Calendar</a>.</p>\n\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}}}s:27:\"http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom\";a:1:{s:4:\"link\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:0:\"\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:1:{s:0:\"\";a:3:{s:4:\"href\";s:35:\"https://theeventscalendar.com/feed/\";s:3:\"rel\";s:4:\"self\";s:4:\"type\";s:19:\"application/rss+xml\";}}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}s:44:\"http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/syndication/\";a:2:{s:12:\"updatePeriod\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:9:\"\n	hourly	\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}s:15:\"updateFrequency\";a:1:{i:0;a:5:{s:4:\"data\";s:4:\"\n	1	\";s:7:\"attribs\";a:0:{}s:8:\"xml_base\";s:0:\"\";s:17:\"xml_base_explicit\";b:0;s:8:\"xml_lang\";s:0:\"\";}}}}}}}}}}}}s:4:\"type\";i:128;s:7:\"headers\";O:48:\"WpOrg\\Requests\\Utility\\CaseInsensitiveDictionary\":1:{s:7:\"\0*\0data\";a:15:{s:4:\"date\";s:29:\"Tue, 27 May 2025 15:34:05 GMT\";s:12:\"content-type\";s:34:\"application/rss+xml; charset=UTF-8\";s:14:\"content-length\";s:5:\"36196\";s:6:\"cf-ray\";s:20:\"946693066ea3006d-CDG\";s:15:\"cf-cache-status\";s:7:\"DYNAMIC\";s:13:\"cache-control\";s:12:\"max-age=3600\";s:16:\"content-encoding\";s:4:\"gzip\";s:7:\"expires\";s:29:\"Tue, 27 May 2025 16:34:04 GMT\";s:13:\"last-modified\";s:29:\"Mon, 26 May 2025 17:23:35 GMT\";s:4:\"link\";s:117:\"<https://theeventscalendar.com/wp-json/>; rel=\"https://api.w.org/\", <https://theeventscalendar.com/>; rel=\"canonical\"\";s:4:\"vary\";s:15:\"Accept-Encoding\";s:9:\"x-nocache\";s:1:\"1\";s:13:\"server-timing\";s:28:\"cfCacheStatus;desc=\"DYNAMIC\"\";s:6:\"server\";s:10:\"cloudflare\";s:7:\"alt-svc\";s:19:\"h3=\":443\"; ma=86400\";}}s:5:\"build\";i:1727736619;s:21:\"cache_expiration_time\";i:1748403244;s:23:\"__cache_expiration_time\";i:1748403244;}', 'off');
